[38;5;252m[1m## Bug Fixed in [38;5;10msrc/rect_pack.rs[0m[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The [38;5;10mfind_just_split[0m heuristic was incorrectly identifying which node was just split during grow operations. It matched nodes by checking [38;5;10m!right.used && !down.used[0m, which could match previously-split nodes with the same structure. This caused duplicate coordinates (e.g., two rects placed at the same position).[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Fix: Changed [38;5;10mgrow_right[0m/[38;5;10mgrow_down[0m/[38;5;10mgrow[0m to return [38;5;10mOption<(i32, i32)>[0m using the already-correct [38;5;10mfind_and_place[0m function, eliminating the buggy [38;5;10mfind_and_split[0m/[38;5;10mfind_and_split_mut[0m/[38;5;10mfind_just_split[0m chain entirely.[0m[0m[38;5;12m[1m✓ Created checkpoint 1

